        "content": "<p>epitaphial opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15294\">issue #15294</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>wasi-preview1-component-adapter: repeated invalid I/O reuses closed streams (EBADF becomes EOF/EIO)</h1>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>On an O_WRONLY descriptor, the second read returns EOF instead of EBADF. On an O_RDONLY descriptor, the second write returns EIO instead of EBADF. No descriptor flags or resource identities change between the two calls.</p>\n<p>Confirmed with the standalone C program below, without any custom test driver or trace format. Each lane reproduced the same output 5/5 times in fresh directories on Wasmtime 46.0.0 (Release and Debug), 47.0.2, and 50.0.1. Wasmtime 50.0.1 was the latest upstream release at verification time.</p>\n<h2>Minimal reproducer (<code>repro.c</code>)</h2>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"C\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;errno.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;fcntl.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;unistd.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">result</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"n\">operation</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">ssize_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rv</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"%s: rv=%zd errno=%d (%s)</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">operation</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rv</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">strerror</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">byte</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">open</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"file.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_CREAT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_TRUNC</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_WRONLY</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mo\">0644</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"initialize: rv=%zd</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">write</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"abcdefghijklmnop\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">16</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">close</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">open</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"file.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_WRONLY</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">ssize_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">read</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"kt\">byte</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first_error</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">ssize_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">second</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">read</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"kt\">byte</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"WRONLY read #1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first_error</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"WRONLY read #2\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">second</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">close</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">open</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"file.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_RDONLY</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">write</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"A\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">first_error</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">second</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">write</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"A\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"RDONLY write #1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first_error</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"RDONLY write #2\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">second</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">errno</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">close</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Exact commands</h2>\n<p>Run in a new empty directory. The first command downloads the official v50.0.1 command adapter; <code>clang</code>, <code>wasm-tools</code>, and <code>wasmtime</code> must be on the stated paths or adjusted to local installations.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code>curl<span class=\"w\"> </span>-fLO<span class=\"w\"> </span>https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/releases/download/v50.0.1/wasi_snapshot_preview1.command.wasm\n/opt/wasi-sdk/bin/clang<span class=\"w\"> </span>--target<span class=\"o\">=</span>wasm32-wasip1<span class=\"w\"> </span>-std<span class=\"o\">=</span>c17<span class=\"w\"> </span>-O2<span class=\"w\"> </span>-Wall<span class=\"w\"> </span>-Wextra<span class=\"w\"> </span>-Werror<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_rc1_closed_stream_reuse.c<span class=\"w\"> </span>-o<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_p1.wasm\nwasm-tools<span class=\"w\"> </span>component<span class=\"w\"> </span>new<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_p1.wasm<span class=\"w\"> </span>--adapt<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">wasi_snapshot_preview1</span><span class=\"o\">=</span>wasi_snapshot_preview1.command.wasm<span class=\"w\"> </span>-o<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_adapter.wasm\nwasmtime<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>--dir<span class=\"w\"> </span>.<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_p1.wasm<span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>wasmtime<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>--dir<span class=\"w\"> </span>.<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_adapter.wasm\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Expected vs. actual output (Wasmtime 50.0.1)</h2>\n<p><strong>Direct P1 (expected):</strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>initialize: rv=16\nWRONLY read #1: rv=-1 errno=8 (Bad file descriptor)\nWRONLY read #2: rv=-1 errno=8 (Bad file descriptor)\nRDONLY write #1: rv=-1 errno=8 (Bad file descriptor)\nRDONLY write #2: rv=-1 errno=8 (Bad file descriptor)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><strong>Adapter P2 (actual):</strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>initialize: rv=16\nWRONLY read #1: rv=-1 errno=8 (Bad file descriptor)\nWRONLY read #2: rv=0 errno=0 (Success)\nRDONLY write #1: rv=-1 errno=8 (Bad file descriptor)\nRDONLY write #2: rv=-1 errno=29 (I/O error)\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Root cause</h2>\n<p><code>Streams</code> retains the <code>InputStream</code>/<code>OutputStream</code> in <code>OnceCell</code>. After the first real I/O error, the host changes the stream to <code>Closed</code> and returns <code>LastOperationFailed(EBADF)</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/v50.0.1/crates/wasi/src/p2/filesystem.rs#L140-L144\">read path</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/v50.0.1/crates/wasi/src/p2/filesystem.rs#L311-L333\">write path</a>). The adapter returns EBADF for that call but leaves the closed stream cached.</p>\n<p>The next call observes only <code>Closed</code>: blocking read maps it to an empty vector/EOF (<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/v50.0.1/crates/wasi-preview1-component-adapter/src/lib.rs#L2601-L2604\"><code>lib.rs:2601-2604</code></a>), while blocking write maps it to <code>ERRNO_IO</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/v50.0.1/crates/wasi-preview1-component-adapter/src/lib.rs#L2629-L2635\"><code>lib.rs:2629-2635</code></a>). The same source paths are present in v50.0.1.</p>\n<h2>Suggested fix and causal evidence</h2>\n<p>Invalidate the corresponding cached stream when <code>LastOperationFailed</code> is returned, so the next P1 operation recreates the stream and rechecks the descriptor. A minimal v46 experiment did this for both read and write. In patch/revert testing, both divergences changed 3/3 → 0/3 → 3/3; reverting restored the original adapter binary. This was a causal experiment, not a proposed complete production patch.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
